{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/feedback/feedback.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T15:38:04.587537Z","id":"379de454b76571ccd4dde45e340a4a7bbca903cc04614faf04c82e9f0b6922f4","body":{"detail":"Chrome binds Ctrl/Cmd+Shift+B to the bookmarks bar and Firefox to the Library; the shell's keydown calls preventDefault, so in the shell that browser key stops working for flagged people. Keys pressed inside the cross-origin artifact frame never reach the shell (web/shell/src/view/keys.ts header), so on an artifact view the shortcut works only with focus in the shell's chrome. The menu (FeedbackMenu.svelte) and the keys sheet show the shortcut either way.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":86},"end":{"line":109},"content_hash":"d91f7aa4dada704e87d209b6a2af8cd97afec173c85b33d2119b6e11aa44dcf8"},"suggested_fix":"If either matters, forward the key from the bridge as `clax:shortcut` does for C (pageKeyAction), or pick a key no browser binds.","summary":"The report shortcut Ctrl+Shift+B (Cmd+Shift+B) takes the browser's own binding while focus is in the shell, and is not heard while focus is in the artifact's frame","tags":["review","feedback-loop","revisit:a flagged person reports the bookmarks bar shortcut lost","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/feedback/feedback.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T16:11:41.991972Z","id":"5fb3737612002719a7db59c9aa55269e99e43ffbf1bf59ce4a58d85b7cd86618","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:81d77e09b","summary":"The report key is now plain F (SHORTCUT in web/shell/src/feedback/feedback.ts), which no browser binds, outside text fields and dialogs; the bridge forwards F pressed in the artifact's frame as it does C (web/bridge/src/channel.ts pageShortcut, web/shell/src/view/keys.ts pageKeyAction, reportKey in web/shell/src/feedback/slot.svelte.ts). Tests: bridge/test/channel.test.ts 'forwards F, the report key...', shell/src/page-shortcut.test.ts 'F pressed in the page starts a report...', shell/src/feedback/feedback.test.ts 'F starts a report...'; //web:unit, //web:e2e_queues and //web:e2e_gesture PASSED.","supersedes":"379de454b76571ccd4dde45e340a4a7bbca903cc04614faf04c82e9f0b6922f4","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/feedback/state.svelte.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T17:44:36.357141Z","id":"8325f7d558a6e159fb6e328b93abaca8f6b8d9f98537a4b64d4ed1cb8dabb0e2","body":{"detail":"The shell's F key is routed to fb.report() through setReportKey (web/shell/src/feedback/slot.svelte.ts); nothing calls setReportKey(null) when the Feedback is closed. Sign-out navigates away, so today the stale hook does not outlive the page, but a close without a navigation would leave F calling a closed overlay.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":21},"end":{"line":21},"content_hash":"758d32a5c5a5dca0475e3d33f9b0eadcdeb3d2f673f2d4062fe48427cb170dc4"},"suggested_fix":"Call setReportKey(null) where the running Feedback is closed.","summary":"setReportKey is never cleared when the feedback integration closes","tags":["feedback","shell","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/feedback/forget.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T17:44:36.357164Z","id":"c8c32afc0e51eef6791ec0ff27d0caaf5f04f3c16139b95d8ab5a148ff7c29ba","body":{"detail":"forgetFeedback races the forgetting against FORGET_TIMEOUT_MS and lets sign-out go on; the work promise is not cancelled, so a slow overlay load can run Clax.forgetReporter (or the running overlay's forget) after the session ended. It touches only this browser's stored key and token, which is what sign-out wants anyway, but its config read then answers for no one. The sign-out test leans on module state (state.svelte.ts's running integration).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":34},"end":{"line":51},"content_hash":"ac968065c69dacb1bf4e15216a4121f475b0508fd850577c3403a5786bf192ba"},"summary":"A forget that times out may still finish after sign-out (local only)","tags":["feedback","shell","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/feedback/feedback.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-07T00:30:28.135907Z","id":"9494a8007fd4f2dca3322156162aae4ddf8cf6769bca8ba38e84e353ab0283cb","body":{"detail":"startFeedback reads the address's fragment once. A reporter sent there signed out signs in first, and whether the fragment lasts through sign-in was not checked: they then reach My reports from the header's menu, which the message names. An overlay on another site ignores the fragment, so crates/clax-server/src/notifiers.rs my_reports sends such a reporter to the page they filed on, unopened.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":187},"end":{"line":191},"content_hash":"58a21d62c9ee127e7a73fbd0d36b946f876787a0785eb61a96e50b51a930070c"},"summary":"/#my-reports opens the reports only for a person signed in when the page loads","tags":["session:claude-code:bd147c0a-6c5a-4917-88d4-4f47695eae89"]}}
